{"id": "school-contracts-signed-before-the-vote", "title": "School contracts: work began months before the board voted, prices just under the bid line", "seconds": 150.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "98283aadb6693d96", "words": 448, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "A school maintenance contract was due to start in July 2023. When did the board see it?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.77, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Work due to start", "1 July 2023"], "b": ["On the board’s agenda", "14 October 2025"], "kicker": "Pacific Northwest Enterprise · $109,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.3, 0.65, 1.03, 1.17, 1.29, 1.38, 1.65, 1.8, 2.11, 2.37, 3.12, 3.63, 3.75, 3.85, 4.12, 4.31]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "836 days later.", "t0": 4.77, "t1": 7.34, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "836 days", "label": "later: 14 October 2025"}, "emph": ["836"], "wt": [0.04, 0.8, 1.17, 1.83, 2.15]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 7.86, "t1": 9.32, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.15, 0.26, 0.81, 0.95, 1.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The first lead. Of 13 sample contracts read, 11 reached the board after their start date.", "t0": 9.54, "t1": 15.28, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "11 of 13", "label": "sample contracts reached the board after their start date", "sub": "median: 105 days"}, "emph": ["11"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.47, 1.13, 1.85, 2.3, 2.58, 3.07, 3.79, 4.16, 4.35, 4.44, 4.71, 4.96, 5.1, 5.33]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "By a median of 105 days. Next longest: Warman Security, 378.", "t0": 15.4, "t1": 20.91, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "11 of 13", "label": "sample contracts reached the board after their start date", "sub": "median: 105 days"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.17, 0.56, 0.7, 0.88, 1.17, 1.48, 2.37, 2.63, 3.13, 3.58, 4.42, 4.61, 4.83]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "A contract that starts first is spent before anyone with authority says yes.", "t0": 21.03, "t1": 24.77, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "spent before anyone with authority has said yes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.55, 0.66, 1.06, 1.38, 1.5, 1.7, 1.99, 2.36, 2.51, 2.99, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The contracts take effect only once approved or ratified, and a board may ratify after the fact.", "t0": 24.89, "t1": 29.63, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "take effect only on board approval or ratification"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.63, 0.78, 1.12, 1.37, 1.58, 1.96, 2.06, 2.88, 2.97, 3.04, 3.32, 3.52, 3.98, 4.22, 4.35]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "And the 2023 one may be a renewal, not a first approval.", "t0": 29.75, "t1": 32.89, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "take effect only on board approval or ratification"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.16, 0.37, 0.85, 1.05, 1.22, 1.3, 1.4, 2.17, 2.3, 2.38, 2.65]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The board’s own pages for seven vendors agree: 74 of 75 dated items put the work first.", "t0": 33.01, "t1": 39.03, "shot": "b5a", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "74 of 75", "label": "dated board items put the work or the processing first", "sub": "median: 45 days"}, "emph": ["74 of 75"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.37, 0.54, 0.91, 1.06, 1.39, 1.79, 2.85, 3.43, 3.64, 4.14, 4.53, 4.87, 5.09, 5.19, 5.48]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[4]", "established[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "They show work begun before the vote, not signatures. The minutes: 49 adopted, none voted down.", "t0": 39.15, "t1": 45.7, "shot": "b5b", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That the contracts were signed before the vote", "The 25 June 2024 consent calendar: listed, no vote recorded"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.26, 0.47, 0.79, 1.05, 1.2, 1.6, 1.8, 2.68, 3.13, 3.67, 4.48, 5.19, 5.4, 5.75]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "In 105 more papers, 29 of 47 first contracts began before the meeting that approved them.", "t0": 45.82, "t1": 51.83, "shot": "b5c", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "29 of 47", "label": "first contracts began before the meeting that ratified or approved them", "sub": "105 more papers: Bay Area Community Resources and Mission Graduates"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.25, 0.6, 0.87, 1.15, 1.93, 2.48, 2.66, 3.2, 3.55, 4.22, 4.65, 4.9, 4.99, 5.29, 5.38, 5.73]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "The second lead. That contract is 109,000 dollars.", "t0": 52.05, "t1": 55.66, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Pacific Northwest Enterprise", "$109,000"], "b": ["Bid limit in its own text", "$109,300"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.4, 0.84, 1.32, 1.78, 1.9, 2.02, 2.24, 2.44, 2.86]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "Its own text states the bid limit: 109,300.", "t0": 55.78, "t1": 60.43, "shot": "b6x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Pacific Northwest Enterprise", "$109,000"], "b": ["Bid limit in its own text", "$109,300"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.33, 0.71, 1.07, 1.17, 1.36, 2.08, 2.22, 2.49, 2.73, 3.35, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "99.7 percent of the line.", "t0": 60.55, "t1": 63.02, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "99.7%", "label": "of the bid limit"}, "emph": ["99.7"], "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.87, 1.27, 1.78, 1.9, 2.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "actors[3]"], "text": "A second contract covers the same door-access upkeep: Warman Security, 114,000 dollars.", "t0": 63.44, "t1": 68.97, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Pacific Northwest Enterprise", "sub": "$109,000, 2023-2026"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Warman Security", "sub": "$114,000, 2024-2027"}], "kicker": "The same door-access and intercom upkeep"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.38, 0.77, 1.03, 1.19, 1.44, 2.06, 2.83, 3.12, 3.83, 3.97, 4.24, 4.64, 4.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Together, 223,000 dollars. 195 percent of the limit.", "t0": 69.09, "t1": 73.63, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$223,000", "label": "together", "sub": "195% of the limit"}, "emph": ["195 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.7, 0.82, 1.05, 1.44, 1.86, 2.68, 2.77, 3.05, 3.52, 3.91, 4.03, 4.19]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Splitting one need between two vendors, each under the limit, avoids the bidding the total requires.", "t0": 74.05, "t1": 78.78, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "avoids the bidding the combined amount would require"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.52, 0.78, 1.1, 1.26, 1.84, 2.03, 2.23, 2.38, 2.85, 3.15, 3.24, 3.55, 3.66, 3.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[1]"], "text": "But services can be contracted without bids, and two vendors may cover different sites.", "t0": 78.9, "t1": 83.02, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "avoids the bidding the combined amount would require"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.47, 0.61, 0.75, 1.27, 1.57, 2.15, 2.34, 2.48, 2.8, 2.95, 3.2, 3.51]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "timeline[3]", "established[1]"], "text": "The third lead. On 9 June 2026, one consent vote approved 41 contracts.", "t0": 83.24, "t1": 89.45, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Item 14, 9 June 2026", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "41 contracts, one consent vote"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.4, 1.13, 2.0, 2.33, 2.64, 2.89, 3.83, 3.98, 4.39, 4.64, 4.98, 5.53]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[1]"], "text": "The item states 26,221,802 dollars.", "t0": 89.57, "t1": 92.77, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["The item’s stated total", "$26,221,802"], "b": ["Its 41 attachments add up to", "$25,825,002"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.38, 0.71, 0.98, 1.53, 1.9, 2.05, 2.47]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[1]"], "text": "The attachments add up to 25,825,002.", "t0": 92.89, "t1": 95.7, "shot": "b12x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["The item’s stated total", "$26,221,802"], "b": ["Its 41 attachments add up to", "$25,825,002"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.63, 0.78, 0.89, 0.98, 1.24, 1.67, 2.02, 2.21]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "The gap: 396,800 dollars.", "t0": 95.82, "t1": 99.29, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$396,800", "label": "the difference", "sub": "exactly the amount of one attachment"}, "emph": ["396,800"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 1.01, 1.16, 1.44, 1.9, 2.31, 2.62, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Exactly one attachment’s amount, perhaps counted twice.", "t0": 99.41, "t1": 102.22, "shot": "b13x", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$396,800", "label": "the difference", "sub": "exactly the amount of one attachment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.47, 0.7, 1.18, 1.78, 2.1, 2.4]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "actors[4]"], "text": "In that vote, Bay Area Community Resources alone had 15 contracts,", "t0": 102.64, "t1": 107.39, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Bay Area Community Resources", "sub": "15 of the 41 contracts, $11,028,600"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.36, 1.01, 1.21, 1.47, 1.94, 2.49, 2.92, 3.3, 3.88]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "actors[4]"], "text": "worth 11,028,600 dollars.", "t0": 107.39, "t1": 109.47, "shot": "b14x", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Bay Area Community Resources", "sub": "15 of the 41 contracts, $11,028,600"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.46, 0.89, 1.53]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "School and City records give it the same address: the same organization.", "t0": 109.59, "t1": 112.87, "shot": "b14y", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["School contracts", "171 Carlos Drive, San Rafael"], "b": ["City contract notices", "171 Carlos Drive, San Rafael"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.37, 0.58, 0.89, 1.04, 1.15, 1.24, 1.46, 2.23, 2.37, 2.58]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The fourth lead. 2 of 50 attachments read leave the price clause unfilled.", "t0": 113.09, "t1": 118.11, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "Board attachments, 2024 and 2026", "text": "INSERT DOLLAR AMOUNT IN WORDS", "mark": "INSERT DOLLAR AMOUNT IN WORDS"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.33, 0.76, 1.26, 1.39, 1.67, 2.44, 2.97, 3.76, 3.86, 4.13, 4.48]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "innocent[2]"], "text": "That leaves the board voting on an amount the papers don’t show.", "t0": 118.23, "t1": 120.71, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "Board attachments, 2024 and 2026", "text": "INSERT DOLLAR AMOUNT IN WORDS", "mark": "INSERT DOLLAR AMOUNT IN WORDS"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.3, 0.38, 0.59, 0.86, 0.97, 1.05, 1.31, 1.47, 1.85, 2.08]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "From May 2024, state advisers could stop board actions that threatened the district’s finances.", "t0": 120.93, "t1": 125.58, "shot": "record-6-May 2024", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fb2", "text": "May 2024", "mark": "May 2024", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.34, 0.49, 1.16, 1.44, 1.88, 2.1, 2.36, 2.63, 3.01, 3.14, 3.4, 3.49, 3.92]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[8]"], "text": "In a separate vote, the Board approved amendments to eight school orders, five to zero.", "t0": 125.8, "t1": 129.52, "shot": "excel-vote", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "excel_signed", "kicker": "Signed resolution · December 16, 2025", "text": "Eight school-specific Mission Graduates orders · vote 5–0", "mark": "5–0"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.13, 0.48, 0.78, 0.86, 1.06, 1.34, 1.8, 1.93, 2.14, 2.48, 2.92, 3.07, 3.23]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[8]"], "text": "The resolution says the original contracts went through bidding.", "t0": 129.64, "t1": 132.24, "shot": "excel-scope", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "excel_signed", "kicker": "Mission Graduates", "text": "Exhibit A · Bryant Elementary CPO26-00113", "mark": "CPO26-00113"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.57, 0.76, 0.9, 1.26, 1.82, 1.95, 2.11]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The records don’t show the gap was a double count, or how common any of this is.", "t0": 132.36, "t1": 136.02, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Whether the $396,800 is a double count in what the board approved", "Whether the door-access contracts were quoted against each other", "How common this is: the contracts are chosen samples"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.37, 0.58, 0.75, 0.87, 1.1, 1.24, 1.3, 1.53, 2.16, 2.25, 2.44, 2.74, 2.96, 3.04, 3.31]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]", "innocent[0]"], "text": "These contracts are samples, not a random draw.", "t0": 136.14, "t1": 138.45, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Whether the $396,800 is a double count in what the board approved", "Whether the door-access contracts were quoted against each other", "How common this is: the contracts are chosen samples"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.53, 0.69, 1.28, 1.47, 1.55, 1.9]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[1]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The 9 June minutes, and the three-quote forms for the door-access contracts.", "t0": 138.57, "t1": 144.25, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The board minutes of 9 June 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "The three-quote forms for the two door-access contracts"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.31, 0.64, 0.97, 1.53, 1.84, 2.05, 2.77, 2.88, 2.98, 3.6, 3.97, 4.08, 4.17, 4.87]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "innocent[2]", "defense[0]"], "text": "A posted copy can be a draft, and no authority has made a finding.", "t0": 144.37, "t1": 147.38, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.47, 0.77, 0.89, 0.97, 1.07, 1.48, 1.6, 1.77, 2.12, 2.29, 2.43, 2.52]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 147.5, "t1": 149.96, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.49, 0.57, 1.38, 1.63, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Due to start", "lead1": "Lead 1 · before the vote", "lead2": "Lead 2 · just under the line", "lead3": "Lead 3 · the total", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the blank price", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "contrast"}